INTERPRETATION
==============

This is a SURPRISE NULL RESULT relative to the A2 prediction ("may
regenerate ALL existing lossy hash-locks; partial probability of
obsoleting W44-117/118/120"). The fix is real (sanity-checked at
the unit-test level — the parity test passes only after the fix is
applied; without the fix it fails by 1.86e1 max-abs) but the buttloop's
decision pipeline is INSENSITIVE to ULP-scale XYB→linear divergences
on the tested cells.

ROOT CAUSE OF INSENSITIVITY (hypothesis):

The buttloop's quant_field convergence depends on `butteraugli(source,
reconstructed)`'s diffmap → median+MAD aggregation. Butteraugli applies:
1. XYB→linear→sRGB-tonemap (us)
2. sRGB→linear→opsin via psychovisual model (Butteraugli internal)
3. Multi-scale Gaussian blur (sigma~1.5 px) on diffmap

The ~5e-6 max-abs perturbation at the input to step (1) is amplified
into ~5e-5 in step (2)'s opsin output, but smoothed below the
median-quantization noise floor by step (3)'s blur. The diffmap's
8x8-block median + MAD then rounds the same integer quant codes for
both the baseline and the fixed paths.

Same insensitivity for SSIM2 loop (uses per-block RMSE on raw XYB
values, not on the reconstructed-vs-source diffmap; RMSE accumulation
over 64 pixels per block washes out 5e-6 per-pixel noise).

NET IMPACT
==========

Code-correctness: GOOD. Our inverse XYB now matches libjxl's reference
formula bit-for-bit (within FMA-association noise; the remaining 3-way
matrix-mul FMA fork is intractable per A2 Fix-4 rejection).

Production bytes: NEUTRAL. No measurable shift on the 8 W44-RECON-DEEP
arc cells. The W44-117/118/120 EPF seed chain is NOT obsoleted by
this fix — they remain load-bearing for the screen-class wedges they
were designed to close. (The "partial obsolescence" prediction in A2
was overstated.)

Hash-locks: BYTE-IDENTICAL. 36/36 lossy fixtures pass without regen.
4/4 Libjxl-strategy byte-locks pass. Drift test 7/7 pass.

Future agents reading this: do NOT cite A2's predicted ~5e-6 perturbation
as a quality bug to chase. It IS measurable in isolation (the parity
test asserts the magnitude) but does not propagate to bytes or
diffmap-derived quant decisions on production-relevant inputs.

